From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] cheetah: allow AppDataBackup in /system

Evolution X installs AppDataBackup in /system, which generic_system.mk's
artifact-path check forbids for device makefiles, so soong_build stops:
"Device makefile produces files inside
build/make/target/product/generic_system.mk's artifact path requirement"
(system/etc/permissions/privapp-permissions-appbackup.xml,
system/priv-app/AppDataBackup/AppDataBackup.apk). AppDataBackup's
skip-on-Pixel check reads PRODUCT_MANUFACTURER, which inherited product
makefiles never see. Allow-list its files, as device/google/shusky does
for husky.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lineage_cheetah.mk | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lineage_cheetah.mk b/lineage_cheetah.mk
index d476562..b6c20c3 100644
--- a/lineage_cheetah.mk
+++ b/lineage_cheetah.mk
@@ -33,4 +33,12 @@ PRODUCT_BUILD_PROP_OVERRIDES += \
     BuildSystemFingerprint=google/generic_system_google/generic:17/CP3A.261005.002.A1/16269273:user/release-keys \
     DeviceProduct=$(DEVICE_CODENAME)
 
+# Evolution X puts AppDataBackup in /system, which generic_system.mk's artifact-path
+# rules forbid for device makefiles (its skip-on-Pixel check reads
+# PRODUCT_MANUFACTURER, which inherited product makefiles never see). Allow it, as
+# LineageOS does for its own /system additions.
+PRODUCT_ARTIFACT_PATH_REQUIREMENT_ALLOWED_LIST += \
+    system/etc/permissions/privapp-permissions-appbackup.xml \
+    system/priv-app/AppDataBackup/%
+
 $(call inherit-product, $(VENDOR_PATH)/$(DEVICE_CODENAME)-vendor.mk)
